From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dinesh Choudhary <idinesh@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:07:33 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] feat(qti): add SAIL communication for resets

Notify the companion SAIL die before powering off or resetting the
system. Nord sends the request through TCSR and waits up to one
second for SAIL readiness before asserting PS_HOLD. Other QTI targets
build no-op implementations. Add Nord's PS_HOLD definition and a
10 ms settling delay before asserting PS_HOLD.

Validation:
- `make -j8 PLAT=nord DEBUG=1` passes.
- QCS615's no-op path compiles; its full build remains blocked by the
  unrelated missing `qti_cpu.h` include in `qti_bl31_setup.c`.

Change-Id: Ib31c117f0877b68227affc03c54f5b12c2eb099e
Assisted-by: GPT-5.6
Signed-off-by: Dinesh Choudhary <idinesh@qti.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://review.trustedfirmware.org/c/TF-A/trusted-firmware-a/+/56540
